    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm hitting a CrashLoopBackOff on a microservice in our GKE cluster and i can't figure out why. here are the logs:\n\ncontainer_log:\n{\"level\":\"error\",\"msg\":\"failed to connect to db: connection refused\",\"timestamp\":\"2023-10-27T10:15:01Z\"}\n{\"level\":\"fatal\",\"msg\":\"shutdown initiated\",\"timestamp\":\"2023-10-27T10:15:02Z\"}\n\ncan u give me a diagnostic checklist to see if this is a resource issue, a liveness probe failure, or something in the config?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
